    {
      "id": 244324,
      "name": "Trajector",
      "username": "Trajector",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/trajector/{size}/1914_2.png",
      "created_at": "2022-04-07T15:53:44.401Z",
      "cooked": "<p>You probably had previously been using an app that had lots of blanket permissions. You just became aware of that fact after Android re-jiggered their permissions requests to be more descriptive at a granular level.</p>\n<p>Have you tried plugging your phone into a PC via USB cable, choosing the option on the phone to let the PC see your phone as a data storage device, and then using Windows File Explorer to navigate your phone’s file system and find the log?</p>\n<p>(Windows File Explorer, of course, will have permission to add, modify, and delete files on your phone. And you won’t be asked if you’re okay with that.)</p>",
      "post_number": 7,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2022-04-07T15:53:44.401Z",
      "reply_count": 2,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
      "reads": 14,
      "readers_count": 13,
      "score": 12.8,
      "yours": false,
      "topic_id": 29234,
